    "question": {
      ":question/id": "dba56e02-9cb1-5240-bc96-6742b38b23af",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(A)=-1$?\n\nI. $A\\text{ is not invertible}$\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$\n\nIII. $A\\text{ does not have }4\\text{ pivot columns}$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=4 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\n$det(A)=-1$, so $A$ is invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)=4$, $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$, $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{4}$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false: $A\\text{ is not invertible}$. $A$ is invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true: $\\text{rank}(A)=4$. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\n- Statement III is false: $A\\text{ does not have }4\\text{ pivot columns}$. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is II only.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
